# Homescool materials (study sheets)

## Product UI (`/homescool`)

- **Left tree** (togglable via DHS first action `Tree`): `ciclo → semana → día → materia → <title>`.
- **Main stage** (right): selected material’s `.page` sections only.
- **DHS Print**: `window.print()` — print CSS hides shell/tree; each `.page` is one PDF page.
- Sheet geometry is **not** rem chrome: US Letter **portrait** (`8.5in × 11in`) or **landscape** (`.page--landscape` / `body.sheets-landscape`). Padding **1cm** (`--page-padding-x/y` in study CSS).

## Authoring CSS / components (reuse)

Canonical stylesheet: `elias/web_assets/styles.css` (served as Homescool `web_assets`). Skill copy: `.eoschool/skill/eoschool/MATERIALS.md` / `TEMPLATES.md`.

| Pattern | Classes | Notes |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Portrait page | `.page` | One print page; `page-break-after: always` |
| Landscape page | `.page.page--landscape` | Letter landscape |
| Quiz page | `.page.page--quiz` | Body: `.quiz-section` + `.quiz.quiz--grid3` |
| Class / lesson page | `.page.page--class` | `.lesson` / `.lesson-section` / `.lesson-text` |
| Checklist page | `.page.page--checklist` | `.checklist-section` + `.checklist` (+ `--grid2` / `--grid3`) |
| Map / board page | `.page.page--map` | `.map-grid`, `.map-grid__board`, `.map-body`; JS `map-grid.js` when needed |
| Header | `.sheet-header` (+ `--compact`), `.meta`, `.student-line` | Title + cycle line |
| Footer | `.sheet-footer` | Page chrome footer |
| Quiz item | `.question`, `.q-num`, `.options`, `.option`, `.opt-key`, `.opt-text` | Never bubble-only options; prefer 12 Q in 3×4 |
| Checklist item | `.checklist__item`, `.checklist__box`, `.checklist__text` | Optional `.checklist-group` |
| Tip block | `.lesson-section--tip` | Callout inside lesson |

When adding a new activity pattern (matching, map grid variant, etc.):

1. Add reusable classes to study `styles.css` (not one-off page CSS).
2. Document the row in this table **and** in `MATERIALS.md`.
3. Keep chrome (`homescool-workspace.css`) rem-only; sheets keep `in`/`pt`/`cm`.

## API / agent

- Docs-first: `GET /api/v1/docs` then `POST /api/v1/homescool/materials` with API key (`api` + `homescool`).
- HTML must use relative `../../../../web_assets/…`; server rewrites to `/api/homescool/web-assets/…`.

## Rem chrome vs sheet units

- Workspace chrome (tree, stage frame, DHS): rem tokens only (`homescool-workspace.css`).
- Inside `.page`: `in` / `pt` / `cm` allowed for print-faithful US Letter (study CSS exception).
